/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   lument_480010465_published_schedule.js — THE ORACLE.

   All 120 rows of Lument Capital's published amortization schedule for
   loan 480010465 (4125 Chestnut), transcribed from the servicer's own
   PDF. This is EXTERNALLY AUTHORED ground truth: nothing in Spine
   produced it, so a derivation that reproduces it is being checked
   against the world rather than against itself.

   ── WHY ALL 120 AND NOT A SAMPLE ────────────────────────────────────
   A first cut of this proof pinned thirteen well-chosen rows — first
   payment, a leap-February, the IO→amortizing transition, the balloon —
   and called the result "the 120-row proof". It was not. It was a
   thirteen-row sample wearing a larger claim.

   The derivation compounds: each row's interest is a function of the
   balance the previous row left behind. A defect at row 67 survives a
   sample that checks rows 1, 49 and 120, and every subsequent balance
   inherits it. Sampling a compounding series proves the endpoints agree,
   which is the one thing a broken middle can still do.

   ── WHAT IT PROVES, AND WHAT IT CANNOT ──────────────────────────────
       PROVES      the contractual calculation — day count, rate,
                   IO→amortizing transition, level payment split,
                   and the remaining principal at maturity
       PROVES NOT  that any of these 120 payments occurred
                   that any of these balances was ever observed
                   that the loan is current

   The schedule proves the arithmetic. The lender statement proves the
   world. Those authorities stay separate inside the tests.

   ── COLUMNS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   As published: [payment_no, due_date, days, interest$, principal$,
   balance_after$]. `days` is the servicer's own "Number Of Days"
   column, not a value this fixture derives. Payments 1–48 are
   interest-only and publish "-" for principal, transcribed as 0, with
   the balance held flat at the original principal. Payment 120 publishes
   "-" for the balance after, transcribed as 0.

   Money is compared in integer CENTS by the harness. Dollars are kept
   here so a human can diff this against the PDF.
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
